{"text": "Ridgeline Building Supply, Inc.\nConfidential HR Incident Report\nField\tEntry\nReport no.\tHR-2026-011\nLocation\tSparks yard, 1890 Glendale Avenue\nIncident date\tMonday, February 9, 2026\nReported by\tMalik Abdi-Rahman, ID 20418\nRespondent\tTravis Boone, ID 17733\nInvestigator\tCharlotte Dubois-Kim, HR Manager\nReport date\t2026-02-13\n\nSummary of the complaint\nMr. Abdi-Rahman, a yard associate hired in June 2024, reports that since December Mr. Boone (known in the yard as \"T.J.\") has made repeated remarks about his religion and background. Malik is Muslim and uses his breaks to pray in the tool crib; he was born in Somalia and became a U.S. citizen last year. He says Boone has called the tool crib \"the mosque,\" asked whether he was \"legal,\" and on February 6 left a printed cartoon taped to his locker (no. 31).\nThe vehicle incident\nAt about 7:15 a.m. on the incident date, Boone reversed the company flatbed (unit 14, Nevada plate 81C 447, VIN 1FDUF5GT4KEC90213) into Mr. Abdi-Rahman's parked Toyota Corolla (plate 392-LMK) while Malik was sitting in it. Boone says it was an accident and that he did not see the car. Malik believes it was deliberate. Damage to the Corolla is estimated at $2,840. Malik was seen the same morning at Truckee Meadows Urgent Care for neck strain and released to light duty; workers' compensation claim WC-NV-0226-5531 has been opened with Sierra Crest Risk Partners and the injury entered on the OSHA 300 log.\nUnder Policy 4.2 Boone took a post-accident drug screen, which came back positive for THC.\nEvidence gathered\nStatement of Guadalupe Santos (\"Lupe\"), forklift operator and shop steward, who heard the \"legal\" remark and saw the cartoon. She asked that her statement be shared with the union under Section 7 of the contract.\nYard camera footage, 7:09 to 7:21 a.m., exported from the recorder (serial DVR-88A41F207).\nPrint log showing the cartoon was printed on February 6 at 6:52 a.m. from the dispatch laptop (asset tag RBS-LT-0462, serial 5CG9413XQ7, IP 10.20.4.117) while signed in as tboone.\nText messages provided by Malik from the number 775-555-0124, which Boone confirms is his.\nInterim actions\nBoone is suspended without pay pending the outcome. Yard supervisor Wade Pruitt has been told to keep the two on separate shifts if Boone returns. Mr. Pruitt admitted that Malik raised the comments with him in January and that he \"told them both to knock it off.\" That is a reporting failure in its own right and will be addressed separately. The conduct described may also raise Title VII concerns; outside counsel has been notified.\nContact\nC. Dubois-Kim, cdubois-kim@ridgelinesupply.example, 775.555.0160, ext. 204. Malik prefers contact by personal email, malik.ar@postmail.example, not through the yard office.", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "441 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Malik Abdi-Rahman", "Travis Boone", "Charlotte Dubois-Kim", "Mr. Abdi-Rahman", "Mr. Boone", "Malik", "Guadalupe Santos", "Wade Pruitt"], "companies": ["Ridgeline Building Supply, Inc.", "ridgelinesupply"]}, "topics": {"places": [], "health": [], "sensitive": [], "names": []}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 1.800000000745058, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "Ridgeline Building Supply, Inc.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Ridgeline Building Supply, Inc."}, {"start": 87, "end": 98, "text": "HR-2026-011", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "HR-2026-011"}, {"start": 121, "end": 141, "t